    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. Governance Test - Missing Named Exports\n**Problem**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `finetune/index.js`, but it was only exported in the default export, causing `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`.\n\n**Solution**: Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) to `finetune/index.js`.\n\n### 2. Eval Test - Metric Parameter Mismatch\n**Problem**: The test expected `toxicity.score` to be 1 (non-toxic), but it was returning 0. The issue was that `runEvaluations()` was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric()` interpreted the second parameter as `bannedTerms` instead of ignoring it. This caused reference strings to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging clean outputs.\n\n**Solution**: Changed `DEFAULT_METRICS` from direct function references to objects with `.evaluate()` methods. Each metric now receives only the parameters it needs:\n- `exactMatchMetric` \u2192 receives (outputs, references)\n- `toxicityMetric` \u2192 receives only (outputs)\n- `lengthVarianceMetric` \u2192 receives (outputs, references)\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests now pass \u2713, and all public exports remain functional.",
